==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Dogenstein]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*1 [[Dober P.D]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Dogenstein]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Dober]] spawns after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>.
*5 [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Dober]] spawns after 143.33 seconds<sup>4,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Cli-One]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Cli-One's purpose is to punish your cats if they push any of the 3 Dobers too far away. Keep in mind that using meatshields in this stage might cause more harm than using none.

Starting with Dogenstein and Dober P.D, you can counter them alone using only [[Can Can Cat]], but it's advised to bring a second damage-dealer just for Dober P.D; almost any [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune attacker]] works, a good choice being [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dancer Cat]]. Afterwards comes St. Dober, who can be beaten with just 2 units: [[Farmboy Cat]] and [[Cafeteria Cat]]. It's still a bit tricky, but manageable; you can bring a 2nd attacker (since Farmboy is here to perma-[[Slow]] him) as long as it meets the [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune]] criterion. As for the final enemy, Dark Dober makes its 7th [[Zero Legends]] appearance and the best way to deal with it is the same as always: Talented [[Dark Lazer]] gets the job done.

